From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dave Stevenson <dave.stevenson@raspberrypi.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Feb 2026 15:52:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gstvideodecoder: Handle DMA_DRM buffers when retrieving vinfo

gst_video_decoder_decide_allocation_default didn't consider the
buffer being a DMA DRM buffer, and got the wrong vinfo.

Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/9247
---
 gst-libs/gst/video/gstvideodecoder.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/gst-libs/gst/video/gstvideodecoder.c
+++ b/gst-libs/gst/video/gstvideodecoder.c
@@ -4273,8 +4273,15 @@ gst_video_decoder_decide_allocation_defa
 
   gst_query_parse_allocation (query, &outcaps, NULL);
   gst_video_info_init (&vinfo);
-  if (outcaps)
-    gst_video_info_from_caps (&vinfo, outcaps);
+  if (outcaps) {
+    if (gst_video_is_dma_drm_caps (outcaps)) {
+      GstVideoInfoDmaDrm drm_info;
+      if (gst_video_info_dma_drm_from_caps (&drm_info, outcaps))
+        vinfo = drm_info.vinfo;
+    } else {
+      gst_video_info_from_caps (&vinfo, outcaps);
+    }
+  }
 
   /* we got configuration from our peer or the decide_allocation method,
    * parse them */
